# Display phase G3: a double-size font, and the resolution and font size are
# remembered on the disk. The framebuffer is write-combining (fast drawing on
# real hardware).
@disk
@args desktop=off
$ display
text: 240x67 characters (8x16 font, automatic)
video memory: write-combining
$ display font 2
text: 120x33 characters (16x32 font)
(saved)
@screenshot 1920x1080 text
$ echo big létters
big létters
$ display mode 1280x720
mode: 1280x720, 32 bits per pixel
text: 80x22 characters (16x32 font)
(saved)
$ cat /system/display
font 2
mode 1280x720
$ display font 3
usage: display font 1|2|auto   (1: 8x16 pixels per character, 2: 16x32)
$ display font
usage: display [mode WIDTHxHEIGHT | font 1|2|auto | test | speed]

# After a restart both are back.
@reboot
$ display
mode: 1280x720, 32 bits per pixel
text: 80x22 characters (16x32 font)
video memory: write-combining
@screenshot 1280x720 text
$ desktop on
desktop on (saved)
$ desktop
desktop: on, the terminal window has 73x18 characters ('desktop off' ends it)
@screenshot 1280x720 pixels 0,0=a8d0f0 1279,719=a8d0f0
$ display font auto
text: 147x37 characters (8x16 font, automatic)
(saved)
$ display mode 1920x1080
(saved)
$ cat /system/display
font auto
mode 1920x1080
